* 2\. History of other malignancies (except cured basal cell carcinoma of the skin and carcinoma in situ of the cervix);
* 3\. Accompanied by other serious diseases, including but not limited to: compensatory heart failure (NYHA grade III and IV), unstable angina, poorly controlled arrhythmias, uncontrolled hypertension (SBP\&gt;160mmHg or DBP\&gt;100mmHg); active infections; unmanageable diabetes mellitus; presence of uncontrolled pleural effusion, pericardial effusion, or ascites requiring drainage; severe portal hypertension; gastric outlet obstruction; Respiratory insufficiency;
